{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-166836-r4518430","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Lentil, Barley, and Tomato Soup","sourcePageId":166836,"sourceRevision":"4518430","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:27:19Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Lentil%2C%20Barley%2C%20and%20Tomato%20Soup&oldid=4518430","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:14.377Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:English recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using barley","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using lentil","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Scottish recipes","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"687546f6f9d23baf662c303f8169ba42d7c93d8a9c16e0f4784722d5aee2facd","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Soup recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United Kingdom|British cooking]]\n\n'''Alexandra soup''' is a puréed vegetable [[Cookbook:Soup|soup]], containing lentils, barley, and tomato. It makes for a warming meal.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 [[Cookbook:mL|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Lentil|lentils]]\n*2 heaped [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] (30 ml) [[Cookbook:Barley|barley]]\n*1 tablespoon (15 ml) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*3 cups (720 ml) [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], peeled, seeded, and diced\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]], to taste\n\n== Preparation ==\n# Soak the lentils and barley together overnight, then drain. This step is optional.\n# [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] the onion in the butter until soft.\n# Add the lentils, barley, and water.\n# Cook until the lentils are tender—this will take longer if grains are not soaked.\n# Add the tomatoes when the soup is almost ready.\n# [[Cookbook:Purée|Purée]] with a food mill, [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]], or [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]].\n# Reheat and adjust the seasoning.\n\n[[Category:English recipes]]\n[[Category:Scottish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lentil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using barley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Lentil, Barley, and Tomato Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup (240 ml) lentils","sourceText":"1 cup (240 ml) lentils","amountText":"1 cup (240 ml) lentils","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 heaped tablespoons (30 ml) barley","sourceText":"2 heaped tablespoons (30 ml) barley","amountText":"2 heaped tablespoons (30 ml) barley","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tablespoon (15 ml) butter","sourceText":"1 tablespoon (15 ml) butter","amountText":"1 tablespoon (15 ml) butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 onion, diced","sourceText":"1 onion, diced","amountText":"1 onion, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"3 cups (720 ml) water","sourceText":"3 cups (720 ml) water","amountText":"3 cups (720 ml) water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"2 tomatoes, peeled, seeded, and diced","sourceText":"2 tomatoes, peeled, seeded, and diced","amountText":"2 tomatoes, peeled, seeded, and diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Salt to taste","sourceText":"Salt to taste","amountText":"Salt to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Pepper, to taste","sourceText":"Pepper, to taste","amountText":"Pepper, to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Soak the lentils and barley together overnight, then drain. This step is optional.","sourceText":"Soak the lentils and barley together overnight, then drain. This step is optional.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Fry the onion in the butter until soft.","sourceText":"Fry the onion in the butter until soft.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Add the lentils, barley, and water.","sourceText":"Add the lentils, barley, and water.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Cook until the lentils are tender—this will take longer if grains are not soaked.","sourceText":"Cook until the lentils are tender—this will take longer if grains are not soaked.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Add the tomatoes when the soup is almost ready.","sourceText":"Add the tomatoes when the soup is almost ready.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Purée with a food mill, blender, or food processor.","sourceText":"Purée with a food mill, blender, or food processor.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":7,"text":"Reheat and adjust the seasoning.","sourceText":"Reheat and adjust the seasoning.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extrac